; Plugin loads, dispatches `(form-arity (point …)) → 3` into
; `wasm:form_arity` and `(forms-arity-sum [(point …) (vec …)]) → 5`
; into `wasm:forms_arity_sum`. Host decodes each result against the
; declared `:result number`. The `(values …)` block locks both arity
; counts so a regression in the §9.1 form payload codec (bare or
; vector-nested) fails loudly.
(diagnostics)
(values
  (value :index 0 :result 3)
  (value :index 1 :result 5))
